 "verdict": "consistent once read from the cipher: 90 signs = 90 letters, 18 groups = 18 words; one letter per shape except the closed-head ε (د x3, ز in حازوا); the cipher reads تخرج ويخرج ويسعوا ... ترجع ويرجع ... تحاسبه مثلما يقعد يحاسبها (q-loop ت for her, d-loop ي for him)",
 "notes": "Rows 2-7 of image 0084_0135: 13 + 16 + 15 + 17 + 15 + 14 = 90, as the record. Plain 1x line crops (x 150-1600) and 1.4x half-line zooms; montages of the look-alikes (cmp_*.png). Two loop-on-a-stem signs are told apart by the stem: the q-loop (stem runs on below the line) is ت (تزوجت twice, تخرج, ترجع, تحاسبه), the d-loop (no descender) is ي (بصبي, يناسبها, في). The d-loop also opens ويخرج, ويسعوا, ويرجع, يقعد and يحاسبها, so the cipher has the masculine verbs: تخرج ويخرج ويسعوا في سباسبها / ترجع ويرجع وقد حازوا مكاسبها تحاسبه مثلما يقعد يحاسبها (\"she goes out and he goes out ... she returns and he returns ... she calls him to account as he sits to call her to account\"). The written text (خزج وخرج ولسعوا ... ورجع ... خاسبه ... تقعد لحاسبها) is a punning or garbled form; the record's own fit already restored the ta-initial verbs. ويسعوا: the fourth sign is the up-left 4-loop that is ع in ترجع, ويرجع, يقعد, not the right-hooked 4-loop ب. ε-hooks: the open one is ز (تزوجت), the closed-head one د in امرد, وقد, يقعد and ز in حازوا."
}